{
  "summary": "This initial experiment established a minimal RNA-only baseline using PCA (2000 components) with a single profile and no image, aggregation, or fusion, yielding a validation accuracy of 0.485 (F1: 0.464). As the first completed trial, this result serves as the performance reference point against which all subsequent design axes—encoder complexity, multiprofile settings, image modality, and fusion strategies—can be comparatively evaluated. It remains uncertain whether any of these additional components can improve upon this floor, and no comparative conclusions about specific design choices can be drawn from a single data point."
}

